s whole loop: the acc64 load, fp32(I), the Sx and Dw loads and broadcasts, the 3-term splits, P, the y terms and y's load and store", "conservative": "I is round-tripped through L1 every block (U6-0's form); qx and qw are loaded, broadcast and widened per tile, where a real kernel can widen once per row and column; FLUSH / 64 is S = ROW at the smallest block count", "excludes": ["bank conflicts (+1 cycle per iteration when two accesses share a 16 KB bank; SILICON.md:85-86), which a static count cannot see", "lock, stream or DMA waits (BENCHMARKS.md:1526-1529)", "code outside the loop"], "deciding": "E_F2 = E_core + FLUSH / 64 (S = ROW at the smallest block count)", "tiers": "E_core > 24: F2-0 KILL (no placement of the flush saves it; F2-E and F2-A are not proposed); E_core <= 24 < E_F2: F2-0 STOP (where the flush runs, the core or the host, comes to the gate; a host flush is priced, its CPU time and the int64 output bytes); E_F2 <= 24: F2-0 PASS (necessary, not sufficient)", "kill_line": 24, "s_set": {"ROW": 64, "16": 16, "8": 8}, "lines": {"break_even_ms": 178.49, "plan_form": {"rule": "18.02 + 6.55 x E < 178.5", "max_e": 24, "role": "DECIDING, fixed as E_F2 <= 24"}, "loop_form": {"rule": "6.55 x (7 + E) < 178.5", "max_e": 20, "role": "sensitivity"}, "serial_form": {"rule": "83.91 + 6.55 x E < 178.5", "max_e": 14, "role": "sensitivity"}}, "model": {"mac_ms": 18.02, "ms_per_cycle": 6.55, "nw4_ms": 83.91, "power_w": 32.78, "m": 2048, "d_nb16_mj": 2.8569, "n_bf16_mj": 2.7417, "sources": "the F2 plan, section 0; docs/BENCHMARKS.md at 554989e; results/llm/llm_prefill3c_posthoc_desktop2_20260924.log:24,25,27"}, "rounding": {"where": "aie::set_rounding(conv_even) once, in f2_flush before its tile loop; f2_block sets none: its srs to int16 (i and P) are at shift 0, exact, so neither the rounding nor the saturation mode changes a value", "source_lines": {"flush_branch": [29], "else": [98, 124, 139], "set_rounding": [57], "flush_loop": [61, 114], "f2_flush": [54], "f2_block"